        "z": "sbf-tab",
        "g": "g-memory",
        "name": "Fire 1/2 then 2/2",
        "info": "SBF framing is length-prefixed, so a block only decodes once its LAST byte arrives. With memory ON (the default) the head waits on the buffer.\n\nTurn memory off with the node below and the same pair produces garbage instead — the head is discarded when the tail arrives.",
